WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.415 --> 00:00:14.697
struggled to free himself from John and Frank.

2
00:00:15.758 --> 00:00:19.381
But they tightened their grips on his wrists and dragged him through the woods.

3
00:00:19.401 --> 00:00:22.183
"Let me go!"

4
00:00:22.684 --> 00:00:23.384
Edward cried.

5
00:00:23.404 --> 00:00:27.048
"Not after all the trouble we had finding you, my boy."

6
00:00:28.348 --> 00:00:30.509
John pinched Edward's arm with his other hand.

7
00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:37.272
"Ow!" Edward tried to kick Tom's father but missed.

8
00:00:37.892 --> 00:00:41.974
"In case you forgot, Ruffler put me in charge of you," Frank said.

9
00:00:41.994 --> 00:00:44.975
"He wasn't happy to hear you'd run off.

10
00:00:46.035 --> 00:00:48.156
From now on, you'll do what I say!"

11
00:00:49.337 --> 00:00:52.498
Edward didn't reply because he was busy plotting his escape.

12
00:00:55.499 --> 00:00:59.213
When they came upon another farmhouse, he hoped this was his opportunity.

13
00:01:00.653 --> 00:01:02.454
But Frank had other ideas.

14
00:01:02.474 --> 00:01:06.096
"Here's your chance to be useful," Frank said.

15
00:01:06.116 --> 00:01:11.138
"Knock on the door, and if someone answers, beg for money or food.

16
00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:15.880
If no one's there, go into the kitchen and steal whatever you can."

17
00:01:18.661 --> 00:01:21.202
Edward grumbled as Frank shoved him toward the house.

18
00:01:21.222 --> 00:01:23.323
"And don't try any tricks!"

19
00:01:23.784 --> 00:01:24.544
Frank called out.

20
00:01:26.088 --> 00:01:28.290
Frank and John watched Edward knock on the door.

21
00:01:30.331 --> 00:01:32.512
When no one answered, he went inside.

22
00:01:32.532 --> 00:01:36.535
"He's not much of a beggar," John said.

23
00:01:36.555 --> 00:01:41.078
"And I need to work with him on stealing, but—" "Quiet!"

24
00:01:41.839 --> 00:01:43.019
Frank held up his hand.

25
00:01:43.039 --> 00:01:45.581
"What's he shouting about?"

26
00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:48.743
"Help! Is anybody home?"

27
00:01:49.183 --> 00:01:49.884
Edward cried.

28
00:01:49.904 --> 00:01:54.647
"I'm King Edward, and I've been kidnapped!"

29
00:01:56.468 --> 00:01:59.529
Frank and John ran for the house and dragged Edward outside.

30
00:01:59.549 --> 00:02:04.311
"That's exactly what I meant by tricks!"

31
00:02:04.792 --> 00:02:05.592
Frank snarled.

32
00:02:05.612 --> 00:02:10.654
"Next time I'll plan my escape more carefully," Edward thought.

33
00:02:10.674 --> 00:02:13.435
"And next time I'll succeed!"

34
00:02:16.997 --> 00:02:20.958
That night at the gang's campsite, Frank stepped on Edward's toes.

35
00:02:22.599 --> 00:02:24.360
Edward knew he'd done it on purpose.

36
00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.483
The third time it happened, Edward confronted Frank.

37
00:02:29.784 --> 00:02:32.006
"Stay away from my feet, you clumsy oaf!"

38
00:02:33.508 --> 00:02:38.092
Edward showered Frank with insults in English, Latin, and Greek.

39
00:02:38.913 --> 00:02:41.795
Everyone gathered around the two of them, clapping and cheering.

40
00:02:41.815 --> 00:02:44.398
"Hooray for the king!"

41
00:02:44.758 --> 00:02:45.339
they shouted.

42
00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:50.544
Two men lifted Edward onto their shoulders and paraded him around the camp.

43
00:02:53.568 --> 00:02:57.730
"Your son has quite a vocabulary," Ruffler said to John.

44
00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:01.772
"I taught him everything I know," John said modestly.

45
00:03:01.792 --> 00:03:05.434
"But I think he picked up a few words from books."

46
00:03:08.176 --> 00:03:11.578
Frank scowled as he watched everyone congratulating Edward.

47
00:03:11.598 --> 00:03:19.382
"I hope that boy is enjoying this," he thought, "because it's the last time he'll humiliate me!"

48
00:03:22.263 --> 00:03:26.601
The next afternoon the gang of beggars and thieves arrived at another village.

49
00:03:26.621 --> 00:03:31.582
"Don't come back empty-handed," Ruffler said to Edward.

50
00:03:31.602 --> 00:03:35.564
"And remember to obey Frank at all times."

51
00:03:39.305 --> 00:03:41.525
Frank walked up and down the streets with Edward.

52
00:03:41.545 --> 00:03:46.947
"Getting arrested might teach our young king a lesson," Frank thought.

53
00:03:46.967 --> 00:03:49.708
"But the others in the gang like him.

54
00:03:50.716 --> 00:03:53.777
So I can't be too obvious about my role in setting him up."

55
00:03:55.278 --> 00:03:59.320
While Frank was plotting his revenge, Edward was looking for a chance to escape.

56
00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:04.342
He thought about running when Frank bent over to pick up a penny on the street.

57
00:04:04.362 --> 00:04:08.104
"Not yet," Edward cautioned himself.

58
00:04:08.124 --> 00:04:11.625
"I have to wait for just the right moment."

59
00:04:13.866 --> 00:04:18.168
A few minutes later, they saw a woman carrying a fat package in a basket.

60
00:04:19.588 --> 00:04:23.552
"Stay here, and don't move until I come back," Frank said.

61
00:04:23.572 --> 00:04:25.853
"This is it!"

62
00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:26.914
Edward thought.

63
00:04:27.895 --> 00:04:32.479
But before Edward could run, Frank sneaked behind the woman and stole her package.

64
00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.421
He thrust it into Edward's hands.

65
00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:37.203
"Don't follow me!"

66
00:04:37.683 --> 00:04:39.625
Frank shouted to Edward as he ran away.

67
00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:41.506
"We'll meet up later."

68
00:04:41.526 --> 00:04:47.892
"No!" Edward threw the package on the ground, where it opened to reveal a ham.

69
00:04:49.796 --> 00:04:50.817
"I am not a thief!"

70
00:04:52.277 --> 00:04:53.458
"Oh yes, you are!"

71
00:04:53.478 --> 00:04:57.940
The woman grabbed Edward and shouted for help.

72
00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:04.202
Meanwhile Frank ran down an alley, from which he gleefully watched Edward's troubles unfold.

73
00:05:05.383 --> 00:05:11.165
"He'll soon be under arrest, and I'll be rid of him for good."

74
00:05:11.565 --> 00:05:15.167
Frank laughed as a blacksmith stepped out of his shop to help the woman.

75
00:05:15.187 --> 00:05:17.448
"What's the matter, ma'am?"

76
00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:21.122
The blacksmith picked up the ham and put it into the woman's basket.

77
00:05:21.142 --> 00:05:26.844
"I was walking home when this boy stole the ham right out of my basket!"

78
00:05:26.864 --> 00:05:29.745
"I am your king, not a thief."

79
00:05:31.266 --> 00:05:33.587
Edward pointed in the direction Frank had fled.

80
00:05:33.607 --> 00:05:36.068
"Quick! Go after Frank.

81
00:05:37.149 --> 00:05:39.290
He's the one who stole your ham!"

82
00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:44.552
"I'd better get out of here before the little traitor leads them to me."

83
00:05:45.504 --> 00:05:47.685
Frank smiled at the thought of Edward in jail.

84
00:05:47.705 --> 00:05:51.888
"Now I just have to think of something to tell Ruffler."

85
00:05:54.369 --> 00:05:57.611
Meanwhile Edward continued to struggle in the woman's grasp.

86
00:05:58.532 --> 00:05:59.552
"Let go of me!"

87
00:05:59.572 --> 00:06:01.714
"Be quiet!"

88
00:06:02.694 --> 00:06:05.536
The blacksmith reached out a strong arm for Edward.

89
00:06:05.556 --> 00:06:08.558
"I'm about to teach you a lesson!"

90
00:06:08.578 --> 00:06:12.040
"You'll do nothing of the kind!"

91
00:06:13.245 --> 00:06:15.089
A man suddenly grabbed the blacksmith.
